  _globals['_TRIGGERSERVICE'].methods_by_name['ListEligibleAccounts']._serialized_options = b'\222A\243\004\n\010Triggers\022$List accounts eligible for a trigger\032\254\003Retrieves the connection\'s accounts, each marked eligible or not for this trigger. An ineligible account is returned with the reason and remedy rather than filtered out, and hidden_count states how many of this connection\'s own accounts were left off the list past the picker\'s cap \342\200\224 never accounts belonging to another connector, which cannot receive this trigger under any configuration and play no part in the count at all.JB\n\003200\022;\n9Successfully retrieved the accounts and their eligibility\202\265\030\033\n\027connected_accounts:read\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002O\022M/api/v1/connections/{connection_id}/triggers/{trigger_name}/eligible-accounts'
  _globals['_TRIGGERSERVICE'].methods_by_name['ListTriggerSubscriptions']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_TRIGGERSERVICE'].methods_by_name['ListTriggerSubscriptions']._serialized_options = b'\222A\200\003\n\010Triggers\022\032List trigger subscriptions\032\217\002Retrieves the trigger subscriptions on a connection, including their status and, for polled triggers, both the requested and the effective interval. Both intervals are returned because a subscription showing only its effective rate is indistinguishable from a broken one.JF\n\003200\022?\n=Successfully retrieved the connection\'s trigger subscriptions\202\265\030\033\n\027connected_accounts:read\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002;\0229/api/v1/connections/{connection_id}/trigger-subscriptions'
  _globals['_TRIGGERSERVICE'].methods_by_name['CreateTriggerSubscription']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_TRIGGERSERVICE'].methods_by_name['CreateTriggerSubscription']._serialized_options = b'\222A\202\004\n\010Triggers\022\026Subscribe to a trigger\032\245\003Subscribes a connected account to a trigger. Every refusal names its remedy: a missing scope names the scope, an interval below the trigger\'s floor names the minimum and what was asked for, and an account authorised under a different app says so. An interval below the floor is refused rather than rounded up, because a customer who asked for 30 seconds and was silently given 300 will build on the number they asked for.J6\n\003200\022/\n-Successfully created the trigger subscription\202\265\030\034\n\030connected_accounts:write\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002>\"9/api/v1/connections/{connection_id}/trigger-subscriptions:\001*'
  _globals['_TRIGGERSERVICE'].methods_by_name['DeleteTriggerSubscription']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_TRIGGERSERVICE'].methods_by_name['DeleteTriggerSubscription']._serialized_options = b'\222A\310\001\n\010Triggers\022\035Delete a trigger subscription\032eRemoves a trigger subscription. Delivery stops immediately; events already handed off are unaffected.J6\n\003200\022/\n-Successfully deleted the trigger subscription\202\265\030\034\n\030connected_accounts:write\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002M*K/api/v1/connections/{connection_id}/trigger-subscriptions/{subscription_id}'
  _globals['_TRIGGERSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetTriggerIngressEndpoint']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_TRIGGERSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetTriggerIngressEndpoint']._serialized_options = b'\222A\213\006\n\010Triggers\022#Get a connection\'s ingress endpoint\032\271\003Retrieves the URL a provider posts events to for this connection, together with whether a signing secret has been set and where any rotation has got to. Use this operation when setting a webhook trigger up: the URL goes into the provider\'s console, and the signing secret must be set before the provider will accept it. The signing secret is never returned \342\200\224 only a masked form, enough to tell which secret is stored without disclosing it.J\246\001\n\003200\022\236\001\njSuccessfully retrieved the ingress endpoint, its masked signing-secret state, and any rotation in progress\0220\n.\032,.scalekit.v1.triggers.TriggerIngressEndpointJu\n\003404\022n\nlNo ingress endpoint exists for this connection - none is minted until an account on the connection activates\202\265\030\033\n\027connected_accounts:read\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\0025\0223/api/v1/connections/{connection_id}/trigger-ingress'
  _globals['_TRIGGERSERVICE'].methods_by_name['SetTriggerSigningSecret']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_TRIGGERSERVICE'].methods_by_name['SetTriggerSigningSecret']._serialized_options = b'\222A\240\t\n\010Triggers\022!Set a connection\'s signing secret\032\342\004Stores the secret the provider signs its events with, taken from the provider\'s own app configuration. Setting a secret where one already exists starts a rotation rather than replacing it: both the old and the new secret are accepted until the rotation is confirmed, so events in flight while the customer updates their provider console are not rejected as forgeries. The response reports the rotation state, including signing_secret_rotation_id; confirm it with ConfirmTriggerSigningSecretRotation, passing that id, once the provider has been updated. The secret is write-only and is never returned or logged.J\235\001\n\003200\022\225\001\naSuccessfully stored the signing secret; the response states whether a rotation is now in progress\0220\n.\032,.scalekit.v1.triggers.TriggerIngressEndpointJH\n\003400\022A\n?The signing secret is empty or longer than the accepted maximumJu\n\003404\022n\nlNo ingress endpoint exists for this connection - none is minted until an account on the connection activatesJ\252\001\n\003409\022\242\001\n\237\001A rotation is already in progress - confirm the current one before starting another, or the secret the customer has just installed would be retired unconfirmed\202\265\030\034\n\030connected_accounts:write\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002G\032B/api/v1/connections/{connection_id}/trigger-ingress/signing-secret:\001*'
  _globals['_TRIGGERSERVICE'].methods_by_name['ConfirmTriggerSigningSecretRotation']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_TRIGGERSERVICE'].methods_by_name['ConfirmTriggerSigningSecretRotation']._serialized_options = b'\222A\312\013\n\010Triggers\022!Confirm a signing-secret rotation\032\352\006Retires the previous signing secret, ending a rotation. Call this once the provider\'s console holds the new secret. Retirement is deliberately explicit rather than automatic: a request arriving under the new secret proves the new secret works, but not that the customer has finished, and a provider that signs some traffic with each would have the old secret withdrawn mid-changeover. Until this is called the previous secret stays accepted, bounded by its expiry so an abandoned rotation cannot leave it valid indefinitely. Pass the signing_secret_rotation_id from the SetTriggerSigningSecret or GetTriggerIngressEndpoint response to confirm that specific rotation. Idempotent: calling this when no rotation is in progress returns the endpoint\'s current state rather than an error, since the caller\'s intent \342\200\224 only the current secret should be accepted \342\200\224 already holds.J\307\001\n\003200\022\277\001\n\212\001Successfully retired the previous signing secret, or confirmed there was none in progress; only the current secret is accepted from now on\0220\n.\032,.scalekit.v1.triggers.TriggerIngressEndpointJ\354\001\n\003400\022\344\001\n\341\001signing_secret_rotation_id does not match the endpoint\'s current rotation - a newer rotation has already started since the caller last read the endpoint\'s state; fetch it again with GetTriggerIngressEndpoint before confirmingJu\n\003404\022n\nlNo ingress endpoint exists for this connection - none is minted until an account on the connection activates\202\265\030\034\n\030connected_accounts:write\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002O\"J/api/v1/connections/{connection_id}/trigger-ingress/signing-secret/confirm:\001*'
